<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 10.255 percent at last week's auction from 10.246 percent at the previous auction on October 23.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 30, 1997 (Jan 23, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.255 percent (10.246)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 855.225 million (984.525 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 893.1 million (1.161 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.150-10.263 percent (10.002-10.276)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.150-10.399 percent (10.002-10.348)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 72 (138)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 79 (159)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
